+ return rows render only after an outbound is picked, which this search must not do.\n\n### When blocked\n\n- Tells of a wall are Access Denied, a captcha, or a results page that never fills.\n- After `link_error`, check the link against the Fastest path, add what is missing, and dispatch once more. After a block or `empty_grid`, do not dispatch the link again. Hand the route to the Google Flights playbook and read Air Canada's rows there.\n- If the page asks for a password, 2FA code, captcha, or payment, stop. Do not solve or bypass. Report which wall appeared and the URL it was on.\n\n## Air Canada booking a picked flight\n\n### When to use\n\nThe user picked an Air Canada flight, from FlightSearch, a card, or the search section, and none of your tools books it in chat. The parent needs the flight numbers and departure time of each leg, the dates, the cabin and fare, such as Economy and Standard, and the count of each traveler type. The search link carries every traveler type as a count, and the passenger page asks each traveler's date of birth. Fill `<CHECKOUT LINK>` with the `checkoutUrl` in the user's Book request only when its host is aircanada.com or a subdomain of it;
